  <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://aidstream.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/documents/Case-Youth-Friendly-services-20240628010647.pdf">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health facilities in Hoima, Uganda provide youth friendly services (YFS)for sexual and reproductive health (SRH) (YFSRH)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Between 2019 and 2021, 15 health facilities in Hoima implemented the adolescent healthimplementation plans they had developed. Some of the actions taken included: holding routine youthdays, during which young people were given priority to access SRH services, providing condomdispensers, peer education programmes at health facilities, maintaining youth friendly corners,development of signposts detailing services offered, and nomination of YFS focal persons. Feedbackon service provision was prioritized by installing suggestion boxes on services accessed by youth.</narrative>
   </description>
   <category code="B01"></category>
   <language code="EN"></language>
   <document-date iso-date="2024-06-28"></document-date>
  </document-link>
  <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://aidstream.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/documents/Case-Youth-Friendly-services-20240628010647.pdf">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ending &#x201c;abstinence only&#x201d; &#x2013; providing quality sexuality education toyouth in Uganda</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2018, youth in 15 Vocational Training Institutions (VTIs) (and from 2019 also youth in fivesecondary schools) received Sexuality Education (SE) beyond &#x201c;abstinence only&#x201d;. They gainedconfidence to discuss their Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR) openly with theirteachers and peers. They also felt confident in seeking SRH services and adopted a safe sexualbehavior. The teachers at the VTIs noted that less female students dropped out due to early andunwated pregnancies.</narrative>
   </description>
   <category code="B01"></category>
   <language code="EN"></language>
   <document-date iso-date="2024-06-28"></document-date>
  </document-link>
